    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0228" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/14966: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vincent</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-25T16:00:00-04:00">March 25, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>400. Embassy’s 398, March 19, 9 a.m. Department would appreciate air mail report
                    in regard to economic concessions granted by Sinkiang to Russia<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d171-f1"/> mentioned in first paragraph of reference telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d171-f1" n="43" xml:id="d171-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 534, April 13, 5 p.m., from the Chargé in China, <ref
                        target="#pg222">p. 222</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
